WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.400
-That's Queen Latifah
right there.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.767
Come on.
-Oh, my God.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:05.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
Hey!

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:07.300
Roots crew.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.133
-Who in the world
is better than you?

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:10.701
You are the best.
You're my favorite.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.567
I want to get into this
and talk about you

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:16.601
for the next 10 minutes.
I want to talk -- the Grammys.

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:19.033
A tribute to hip hop.
50 years of hip hop.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.801
You crushed it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:22.601
-Oh, thank you.
-You were unbelievable!

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:25.501
Came out, smoke and everything.

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.067
Did you --
Did you feel the vibe?

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:28.567
-Did you see me smoking?
-No, no, no.

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:30.234
-Oh, okay, okay.
-I just saw smoke come out

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:32.400
when you came out.
-I'm just joking.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.767
-Did you feel the vibe
when you were performing?

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.267
Could you see
what we saw at home?

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.601
-I feel like
I've been seeing them for days

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:39.667
after days after days.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:41.234
-They did a great job,
The Roots.

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:43.434
-Thank God, who else could pull
off that but the Roots crew?

00:00:43.434 --> 00:00:44.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Nobody could do that.

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:46.934
-Thanks, Quest.
Oh, my God -- Tariq.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.234
I don't know who else
could pull that off.

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:50.601
It was amazing.
It was --

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:52.067
-People were dancing
and going nuts.

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:53.400
And you kind of opened up
the party.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.567
It was awesome.
I was like --

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:56.300
-People went off.
And I heard they brought out

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.734
champagne after, you know, after
the hip hop segment itself.

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.467
-Is that right?
-So, it was definitely,

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.033
you know,
cracking in that audience.

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:05.400
-Yeah, everything got that.
They got the party going, yeah.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.934
What was it like to be on stage
with all these -- look at this.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.367
-It was so crazy.
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:12.234
-Just generations --
-I mean, you got L,

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:14.801
you got Public Enemy.
You know, um --

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:17.434
There's so many people
on this stage who, without them,

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:20.200
I would not be here.
Like, just Melle Mel,

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.234
Grandmaster Flash,
the Furious Five.

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:26.100
Like, you know...
♪ Don't push me 'cause I'm -- ♪

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:29.100
Come on now. Like,
everybody knows that record.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.968
And I remember being like 15
in Latin Quarters

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:35.968
watching Melle Mel on the stage,
rhyming for 20 minutes straight.

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:38.167
And then, KRS-One trying
to get the mic from him.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.200
And, like,
this is hip hop history.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.534
Like, I wouldn't know anything
if Public Enemy

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:43.801
didn't take me out on tour.

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:45.901
Like, I was
a baby act on their tour.

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:47.100
-How old were you
when you were on tour with --

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.667
-I was like 17 or 18 years old.

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:51.901
I had, like,
one record out, maybe.

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.267
You know what I mean?
-What were they like?

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:56.000
-They were like uncles.
Honestly, some people

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.234
are selfish in this business,
as we know.

00:01:58.234 --> 00:01:59.467
They were not that.

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:03.067
They wanted to share
the information, teach us.

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:05.033
'Cause they know
we didn't know anything.

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:06.567
You know, so, instead of,
like, you know,

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:09.133
keeping it all to themselves,
they showed us how to move

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:12.000
and shake on the road, how to
kind of prepare ourselves,

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.234
where to be on the stage,
how to use -- hold the mics,

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:19.100
and how to do business
with the promoters

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.434
'cause that's always tricky.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:24.300
And really, like,
helped us to learn

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.300
so that we could grow
and start our own businesses.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.534
Because we're all little,
tiny businesses,

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:30.100
you know, at the time.
-Yeah.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.067
Who said to you something like,

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:33.434
"I remember
when you had a drum set."

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:36.701
-Oh, that was Method Man.
Yo, give it up for everybody

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:38.234
that was on the stage
that night.

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:39.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
Everybody.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:42.167
-It was insane!
It didn't stop.

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:44.501
-Yo.

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:46.701
And to watch everybody
right now, like,

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:49.767
going into all these careers
from rap -- from one rap record

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:53.167
to, you know, actors
and nominated and all this

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:56.300
and talk shows.
This is just amazing, you know,

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.801
how hip hop
has just become global.

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:00.434
Which we always knew
it would be,

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:02.334
but the world --
They fought us, you know?

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:05.167
They wanted to censor us.
I mean, we had to go to court

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:07.601
not to be censored.
Thanks, Luke.

00:03:07.601 --> 00:03:09.834
-Yeah, right.
-Ice-T told me

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.601
how to move and shake in L.A.,
you know,

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:14.701
when it was very ganged up.
You know what I mean?

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:16.200
Like, "You don't know anything.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.601
Get behind this wall
real quick."

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.434
-Yeah,
"You don't see nothing, bud."

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:20.934
Did you think that it wasn't --
-But it was Method Man.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.934
Method remembers everything.

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:26.067
He was like, "I remember seeing
you at Madison Square Garden.

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:28.567
You was opening up for
Public Enemy, matter of fact.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.367
And you had a drummer.

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.000
And nobody else had a drummer."

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.801
And I was like,
"Yeah, I had a drummer."

00:03:33.801 --> 00:03:36.267
-You wanted that live element?
-I wanted that vibe.

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:38.601
I wanted to add on to it,
and nobody was doing it.

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:42.734
And then, I took the Fugees out
on their first tour.

00:03:42.734 --> 00:03:44.934
Fugees went way beyond
a drummer.

00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:48.868
Like, the Fugees was like,
"Okay. We can do that?

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:51.701
Watch this."
And they really went crazy.

00:03:51.701 --> 00:03:54.901
So, like, we all have shared
things with each other

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:57.167
that have taken this hip hop
thing to a whole nother level.

00:03:57.167 --> 00:04:01.434
-Whole new level. Did it remind
you of when you won a Grammy?

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:04.834
-Well, unfortunately, I wasn't
there when I won my Grammy.

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:06.767
We weren't even televised
at the time.

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:08.734
-No.
-So, I won my first Grammy

00:04:08.734 --> 00:04:11.968
for "U.N.I.T.Y.," first
Rap Female Solo Performance.

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:13.200
-I mean, come on.
Absolutely.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.033
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:16.801
-But even then --
-They didn't televise it?

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:19.167
-No.
So, even that, it shows you how

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:22.267
the Grammys have evolved
because rap was not even

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:24.767
a televised category.
Can you imagine?

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:27.834
Like, it wasn't even --
None of it was even on TV.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:30.033
It was like, "Is this a fad?
Is this real?

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:31.267
Should we make it a category?"

00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:33.501
Like, we were fighting
to become a category.

00:04:33.501 --> 00:04:35.968
So, we are way beyond
a category now.

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:39.901
And you can see hip hop has
influenced all sorts of music,

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:43.934
not just, you know, rap or R&amp;B,
but it's all in pop music.

00:04:43.934 --> 00:04:46.367
It's all in country music.
It's everywhere now.

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:47.834
-Yeah. You know
what I thought was fun, too?

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:50.567
Jay-Z obviously
could have gotten on stage.

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:52.300
He could've rapped --
-Man, Jay was having so much fun

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.634
in that --
Did you see him?

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:56.567
-He was like a little kid.
He was like, "Oh, my God!"

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:58.167
You never
get to see him like that

00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:00.067
'cause he's always
just being cool.

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:02.334
He was, like, fanboying out.
-Yes.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:05.167
-I love seeing that.
It just made you so happy.

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:06.367
Like, "Oh, he's doing
what we're all doing."

00:05:06.367 --> 00:05:07.767
-Yeah, we laughed at that
afterwards.

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:09.834
Like, yo -- he was like,
"Remember us in Mars,

00:05:09.834 --> 00:05:11.834
these little clubs?"
He was thinking about all --

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:13.701
'Cause we --
I mean, none of us had --

00:05:13.701 --> 00:05:15.601
We come from, like, nothing.
You know what I mean?

00:05:15.601 --> 00:05:19.367
And then we got this music
that has taken us everywhere.

00:05:19.367 --> 00:05:22.334
So, I think he was seeing
his favorites out there, too.

00:05:22.334 --> 00:05:24.534
And it just was, like,
so much fun.

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:27.267
And LL, of course --
thanks, L, for, just, like --

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:28.934
-He's -- come on.
-I think L --

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:30.901
L might've had
all of us in a headlock.

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:34.033
He was like, "This thing
ain't happening without me.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.501
Let me tell you something.
Don't call it a comeback."

00:05:36.501 --> 00:05:38.067
-Oh, yeah, come on!
-Oh, man.

00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:40.501
When "Rock the Bells" dropped,
I was like, "Let the beat drop!"

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:41.934
-Yeah!
-I was goin' crazy.

00:05:41.934 --> 00:05:43.434
-L.L., come on.
-You see that radio?

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:45.067
-Yeah.
-That blinged-out radio?

00:05:45.067 --> 00:05:46.200
I want that radio.
-It was blinged out.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.234
-By the way,
I want that radio, too.

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:48.567
-I want that radio.
I can't front.

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:50.334
-We'll share it.
We'll share it.

00:05:50.334 --> 00:05:52.234
I quickly want to mention this.

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:54.234
You have a new
Audible original here.

00:05:54.234 --> 00:05:57.701
-This is amazing.
-"Unity in the Community."

00:05:57.701 --> 00:05:59.267
I love that you did this.

00:05:59.267 --> 00:06:02.000
How do you explain that?
It's seven episodes?

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:05.367
-It's a seven-part series.
It's seven episodes.

00:06:05.367 --> 00:06:08.567
It's an Audible original.
I am narrating it.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.834
You will hear me
be the voice of Unity.

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:12.300
Let me hold on
to that for a second.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.701
-Yeah.
-That's just so nice.

00:06:13.701 --> 00:06:15.400
-That's so nice.
-Look at that.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
Look at that.

00:06:17.234 --> 00:06:19.834
You know?
The colors.

00:06:19.834 --> 00:06:22.200
The joy.
It's just a --

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.400
-Come on.
-You just feel the love.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.834
-Yeah.
-But you know what?

00:06:25.834 --> 00:06:29.067
This is -- This tells seven
stories of different people

00:06:29.067 --> 00:06:31.167
who saw something
that needed to change

00:06:31.167 --> 00:06:33.400
and decided that they were
gonna be that change.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.701
So, whether it was deciding
that, "Oh, okay.

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:38.467
I know how to cook,
I have a restaurant,

00:06:38.467 --> 00:06:40.300
and people are hungry,
and it's COVID.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:42.868
I'm gonna feed people."
And they did that.

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:47.200
Or whether it's someone who is
of Japanese descent

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:51.868
and is trying to preserve
Little Tokyo and its history,

00:06:51.868 --> 00:06:53.467
she did that, you know?

00:06:53.467 --> 00:06:56.434
Whether it's someone Native
who is trying to preserve a park

00:06:56.434 --> 00:07:00.734
in Chicago and that culture,
they did that.

00:07:00.734 --> 00:07:02.334
-It's inspiring.
-It's so --

00:07:02.334 --> 00:07:04.601
It's all these
inspiring stories.

00:07:04.601 --> 00:07:07.868
And I got to tell you,
just reading it myself,

00:07:07.868 --> 00:07:11.701
I was so inspired
listening to it, reading it,

00:07:11.701 --> 00:07:15.000
hearing their stories that I
think you're gonna love this.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.234
So, it's out right now.
Check it out on Audible.

00:07:17.234 --> 00:07:21.634
And please just -- especially,
if you're feeling good, cool.

00:07:21.634 --> 00:07:22.868
But if you're not feeling good,

00:07:22.868 --> 00:07:24.434
and you want to feel good,
listen to that.

00:07:24.434 --> 00:07:26.000
-"Unity in the Community"
right there.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.400
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:30.367
We are the community.
-U-N-I-T-Y.

00:07:30.367 --> 00:07:34.267
-That's our unity.
-I want to -- [ Laughs ]

00:07:34.267 --> 00:07:36.000
I want to talk about
"The Equalizer."

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.968
Come on! Let's talk about this.
-Okay.

00:07:37.968 --> 00:07:40.167
So, now we switch from "unity"
to "you're wanted with me."

00:07:40.167 --> 00:07:42.601
-Yeah, exactly, okay.
